{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"110603","commit":"f51dd2cd5350241e08accfe888e0c06d72861868","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `useTsdbDefaults` field is declared and initialized to `false`, but it is never read or used anywhere in this chapter. In `#YPDFZ`, the default-mapping merge is gated only on `indexSettings.getMode().getDefaultMapping() !\u003d null`, with no reference to `useTsdbDefaults`. If this field is intended to let individual tests opt out of the default-mapping merge (e.g., to test the \"no `@timestamp` mapper\" path), the gating logic in `build()` is missing. If it is used in a later chapter, that\u0027s fine, but as it stands in this chapter it is dead code.","nodes":[{"id":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java-test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java--10168:10200","promptId":"#KZEQP","srcPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java","dstPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10168,"endPos":10200,"startLine":228,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":228,"endLineOffset":40,"length":33}]},{"id":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java-test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java--10507:10531","promptId":"#9Z9YE","srcPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java","dstPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10507,"endPos":10531,"startLine":236,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":236,"endLineOffset":36,"length":25}]}]},{"comment":"There is an inconsistency in which document context is used to access the keyed field. `#QFEZC` writes the key via `context.doc().onlyAddKey(...)`, `#0KTA1` reads it via `context.doc().getByKey(...)`, but `#S02V5` reads it via `context.rootDoc().getByKey(...)`. In the current call paths both resolve to the same root `LuceneDocument`, so the behavior is correct today. However, if a future change ever introduces a nested-document context where `doc() !\u003d rootDoc()`, `#S02V5` would silently get `null` while the other two would still work (or vice-versa). Picking one convention (`rootDoc()` for both readers, since the key is always written at the root) would make the contract explicit and prevent a subtle bug.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-1989:1997,1998:2041-1989:1997,1998:2048","promptId":"#S02V5","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":1998,"endPos":2041,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":73,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":116,"length":44}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":1998,"endPos":2048,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":73,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":123,"length":51}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java--38570:38662,38671:38728,38737:38791,38800:38802,38811:38872,38881:38942,38951:40010","promptId":"#QFEZC","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":38570,"endPos":38662,"startLine":950,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":950,"endLineOffset":100,"length":93},{"pos":38671,"endPos":38728,"startLine":951,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":951,"endLineOffset":65,"length":58},{"pos":38737,"endPos":38791,"startLine":952,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":952,"endLineOffset":62,"length":55},{"pos":38800,"endPos":38802,"startLine":953,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":953,"endLineOffset":10,"length":3},{"pos":38811,"endPos":38872,"startLine":954,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":954,"endLineOffset":69,"length":62},{"pos":38881,"endPos":38942,"startLine":955,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":955,"endLineOffset":69,"length":62},{"pos":38951,"endPos":40010,"startLine":956,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":972,"endLineOffset":9,"length":1060}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-8348:8386,8410:8415,8418:8422,8432:8498,8507:9170,9184:9189,9555:9560-8459:8477,8480:8534,8544:8717,8727:8808,8821:8840,9207:9253","promptId":"#0KTA1","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":8348,"endPos":8386,"startLine":198,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":198,"endLineOffset":46,"length":39},{"pos":8410,"endPos":8415,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":23,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":28,"length":6},{"pos":8418,"endPos":8422,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":31,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":35,"length":5},{"pos":8432,"endPos":8498,"startLine":200,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":200,"endLineOffset":74,"length":67},{"pos":8507,"endPos":9170,"startLine":201,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":215,"endLineOffset":9,"length":664},{"pos":9184,"endPos":9189,"startLine":217,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":217,"endLineOffset":17,"length":6},{"pos":9555,"endPos":9560,"startLine":223,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":223,"endLineOffset":43,"length":6}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8459,"endPos":8477,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":23,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":41,"length":19},{"pos":8480,"endPos":8534,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":44,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":98,"length":55},{"pos":8544,"endPos":8717,"startLine":200,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":202,"endLineOffset":9,"length":174},{"pos":8727,"endPos":8808,"startLine":204,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":204,"endLineOffset":89,"length":82},{"pos":8821,"endPos":8840,"startLine":205,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":205,"endLineOffset":31,"length":20},{"pos":9207,"endPos":9253,"startLine":212,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":212,"endLineOffset":84,"length":47}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":956,"line":955,"comment_lines":["[][955]"],"review_comment":["This `isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled` check is unfortunate. The reason for it being here is that we can\u0027t fully trust `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream`. In its current implementation `isDataStream` starts as `false` and then gets flipped to `true` if `DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper` is enabled in **current** mapping. This is broken for an edge case of a mapping overriding default `@timestamp` mapping (it is more generally broken for any mapping updates but this is the first time we experience that).\r\n\r\nScenario:\r\n1. Create a time series index with default mapping only\r\n2. Update mapping with\r\n```\r\n{\"@timestamp\": {\"type\": \"date\"}}\r\n```\r\nFor this mapping update `isDataStream` is `false` even though it was `true` previously.\r\n\r\nOne option to fix this is to pass existing mapping into `MappingParser#parse` and initialize `isDataStream` to a value based on it. I didn\u0027t want to mix this change in here.","Thanks for this explanation. Let\u0027s make fixing `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream()` a followup of this change. As part of that change the ` \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()` part of the condition can be removed."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","id":36737,"created_at":"2024-07-08T21:33:57Z","original_position":55,"side":"RIGHT","position":47,"submitted_on_commit":"f51dd2cd5350241e08accfe888e0c06d72861868","diff_hunk":"@@ -942,6 +947,30 @@ protected void parseCreateField(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOExceptio\n     }\n \n     private void indexValue(DocumentParserContext context, long timestamp) {\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper and TsidExtractingFieldMapper need to use timestamp value,\n+        // so when this is true we store it in a well-known place\n+        // instead of forcing them to iterate over all fields.\n+        //\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper is present and enabled both\n+        // in data streams and standalone indices in time_series mode\n+        if (isDataStreamTimestampField \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()) {","submitted_line":956},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"There is an inconsistency in which document context is used to access the keyed field. `#QFEZC` writes the key via `context.doc().onlyAddKey(...)`, `#0KTA1` reads it via `context.doc().getByKey(...)`, but `#S02V5` reads it via `context.rootDoc().getByKey(...)`. In the current call paths both resolve to the same root `LuceneDocument`, so the behavior is correct today. However, if a future change ever introduces a nested-document context where `doc() !\u003d rootDoc()`, `#S02V5` would silently get `null` while the other two would still work (or vice-versa). Picking one convention (`rootDoc()` for both readers, since the key is always written at the root) would make the contract explicit and prevent a subtle bug.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-1989:1997,1998:2041-1989:1997,1998:2048","promptId"